#1779 added tests/test_no_committed_dependency_pins.py without a
`# covers:` marker. Its name maps to no top-level source, so
test_top_level_test_map's ratchet (test_no_new_unreachable_top_level_tests
and test_the_exempt_list_is_empty...) has been red on dev since it merged:
#1779's CI selected only the new test, not the ratchet. Found while
running smart-test for the WI-zomif branch.

The marker declares `*requirements*.txt`, which the route-parity
fixtures match. Lockfile globs cannot be declared:
test_no_declared_glob_has_rotted rejects a glob matching no tracked
file, and keeping that set empty is this test's purpose. So per-PR CI
selects it on a requirements change; a newly committed lockfile is
caught by the full-suite cron, which runs every root test. The header
says so.

tests/test_top_level_test_map.py: 51 passed with the change. The
ratchet file is added to this PR's manifest so CI runs it.

